@startuml
title US13 - List Employees by Role\nClass Diagram (CD)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam classBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

class Employee {
    - code : wstring
    - name : wstring
    - role : wstring
    --
    + Employee(code, name, role)
    + getCode() : const wstring&
    + getName() : const wstring&
    + getRole() : const wstring&
}

class EmployeeRepository {
    - employees : vector<Employee>
    --
    + add(employee) : bool
    + findByRole(role) : vector<Employee>
    + existsByCode(code) : bool
    + count() : size_t
}

class ListEmployeesByRole {
    - repository : const EmployeeRepository&
    --
    + ListEmployeesByRole(repository)
    + execute(role) : vector<Employee>
}

EmployeeRepository "1" o-- "0..*" Employee : stores

ListEmployeesByRole --> EmployeeRepository : queries

note right of ListEmployeesByRole
US13 - List Employees by Role

Returns employees matching
the selected role.

The operation is read-only.
end note

note bottom of EmployeeRepository
Currently uses in-memory storage.

Role comparison is exact
and case-sensitive.
end note

@enduml